<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharur District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharur is a district of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a> Autonomous Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, in the fertile plain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Aras River</a> near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. In 1501 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sharur">Battle of Sharur</a>, a step towards founding the Safavid state. After 1918 the district was disputed between Armenia and local Muslim governments such as the Republic of Aras.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharur-district.jpg" alt="Sharur District" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NordNordWest, edited by Toghrul R · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharur_District_in_Azerbaijan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
